$readme$),
        ('cobalt', 'template', $readme$# Cobalt::Template

A logic-light text templating engine. Everything is explicit: no hidden allocation, no global state.

## Installation

```sh
rux add Cobalt::Template
```

## Usage

```rux
import Cobalt::Template;

func Main() -> int {
    let result = Template::Compile("^a.*z$")?;
    Print(result.Matches("abcz"));
    return 0;
}
```

## Features

- Correct handling of multi-byte code points
- Borrowed slices instead of copies
- Linear-time matching with no backtracking
- Locale-independent behaviour by default

## Design

The implementation favours a single obvious path over a configurable one. Where a knob would only exist to paper over a bad default, the default was fixed instead. The result is a smaller API surface, fewer states to test, and behaviour that is the same on every platform.

## Compatibility

Tested against the last two stable Rux releases. Nightly builds are exercised in continuous integration but not supported.

